meta {
  name: 35 List Report Notes
  type: http
  seq: 35
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/lab-reports/{{labReportId}}/notes
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  ~category: SAMPLE
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  Order Notes / Sample Notes / Tech Notes tabs of the Test Entry popup and the
  Order ID popup (LABORATORY.docx §4.2), plus the worklist's notes hover cards.
  Newest first (`createdAt` descending).

  The list is ORDER-WIDE: it covers every live report of this report's order in
  the caller's active branch, so any test of the order can be the anchor. Each
  row: `{ id, tenantId, labReportId, category, body, createdBy, createdByName,
  createdAt, deletedAt, testName, sampleLabel }`.

  - `labReportId` — the report the note was written on.
  - `testName` — that report's test (a panel member's own test name).
  - `sampleLabel` — that report's sample(s) as `"<sample name> · <barcode>"`,
    comma-separated when the test has several samples; `null` when none.
  - `createdByName` — the author's resolved name (falls back to the raw
    `Person.id`).

  Query params:
  - `category` (optional) — `ORDER` | `SAMPLE` | `TECH`. Omit for all three.
    Workflow reasons (Lock, Delta, Re-Run, …) are never listed.

  The worklist row's `noteCounts` (`GET /lab-reports`) and the Order Console
  (`GET /orders/:id/notes`, source `LAB_REPORT`) read these same notes.

  Allowed on a locked, sent-out or cancelled test (a read). 404
  `LAB_REPORT_NOT_FOUND` if the report is missing, another tenant's, or held by
  another branch.
}
